{"type":"standard","title":"Ila language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ila language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q5996885","titles":{"canonical":"Ila_language","normalized":"Ila language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ila language</span></span>"},"pageid":33621077,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1336410387","tid":"4c8dae41-0124-11f1-8ef9-e9f782e35146","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:18:04Z","description":"Bantu language spoken in Zambia","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ila_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ila_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ila_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ila_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ila_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ila_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ila_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ila_language"}},"extract":"Ila (Chiila) is a language of Zambia. Maho (2009) lists Lundwe (Shukulumbwe) and Sala as distinct languages most closely related to Ila. Ila is one of the languages of the Earth included on the Voyager Golden Record.","extract_html":"<p><b>Ila</b> (<i>Chiila</i>) is a language of Zambia. Maho (2009) lists <b>Lundwe</b> (<i>Shukulumbwe</i>) and <b>Sala</b> as distinct languages most closely related to Ila. Ila is one of the languages of the Earth included on the Voyager Golden Record.</p>"}